{"report":{"plan":{"study":{"schema":"frontier/foundry-study-v1","runtime":"alpha-genesis-harness@0.3.0","hypothesis":"Named reuse increases accepted construction for a continuation decision compared with equal-content ordinary reuse.","model":"qwen3-4b-instruct-2507-q4_k_m","output_tokens":256,"task":{"acceptance":"Every held case must agree with the independent decision. No network or file effects from the evaluator.","alternative":"Direct Python range membership/cardinality with source checks for strong ETag and byte counts.","inputs":{"body_bytes":{"max":2000000000,"min":0},"end":{"max":2000000000,"min":0},"object_bytes":{"max":2000000000,"min":0},"previous_end":{"max":2000000000,"min":0},"same_version":"boolean","start":{"max":2000000000,"min":0}},"language":"en","objective":"Decide whether a fresh partial weather-data response can extend the last verified prefix.","outputs":{"appendable":"boolean"},"rule":"All inputs except same_version are nonnegative integers. previous_end is the last saved byte. start and end are inclusive offsets in the new response, object_bytes is the total object length, and body_bytes is the integer count of bytes actually transferred. same_version means the same strong version validator. Output appendable is true exactly when same_version is true, start is one after previous_end, start is at or before end, end is within the object, and the inclusive count of the new interval equals body_bytes. Offsets start at zero. The last legal offset is object_bytes minus one. An end offset equal to object_bytes must be rejected, even if the lengths agree.","schema":"frontier/foundry-mission-v1"},"suite_sha256":"caf08d824b7d4752886501a679be79074a711b9818af17b5e344fa444127052a","parent":{"asset":{"candidate":{"inputs":["end","start"],"name":"s1-formulas","outputs":{"bytes":{"args":[{"args":[{"field":"end"},{"field":"start"}],"op":"sub"},1],"op":"add"},"ordered":{"args":[{"field":"start"},{"field":"end"}],"op":"lte"}}},"candidate_sha256":"b37b5c4dfb